Licensing overview for nfdi4sd
==============================

This repository is multi-licensed. There is no single license that covers all
of it, because the example model is derived from a third-party work whose
license carries over.

Machine-readable licensing information is in REUSE.toml, following the REUSE
specification (https://reuse.software/). Full license texts are in LICENSES/.
Verify with `reuse lint`.

  Code                                          MIT
  runners/, scripts/, tests/, Snakefile,
  .github/, repository metadata

  Documentation                                 CC BY 4.0
  README.md, CHANGELOG.md, docs/*.md

  Kaibab example model and derivatives          CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  models/, config/, docs/kaibab_example.md,
  docs/kaibab_ecosystem_report/,
  docs/kaibab_variable_description.xlsx

Why the three licenses exists
-----------------------------

The Kaibab ecosystem model in this repository is a re-implementation of the
model published as Exhibit 4.11 of:

  Deaton, M., & MacDonald, R. (2025). System Dynamics Learning Guide,
  Chapter 4, Section 4.11. James Madison University Libraries.
  https://pressbooks.lib.jmu.edu/sdlearningguide/

That work is licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, and the model files reproduce parts of
its text (variable descriptions). ShareAlike therefore requires that the model
files and anything derived from them carry the same license, and NonCommercial
restricts their use.

What this means for you
-----------------------

  - You may use the structure, the workflow and the code of this repository
    for any purpose, including commercially, under the MIT license.
  - You may reuse the documentation with attribution under CC BY 4.0.
  - You may NOT use the Kaibab model files commercially, and any adaptation of
    them must be shared under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

If you want an unencumbered version, replace the example model with one that is
not derived from a NonCommercial source. The repository structure and workflow
do not depend on the Kaibab model.

Note: GitHub's automatic license detection will not report a single license for
this repository, and that is intentional.

